website/versioned_docs/version-stable/options.md:213:Both the `babel` and `flow` parsers support the same set of JavaScript features (including Flow type annotations). They might differ in some edge cases, so if you run into one of those you can try `flow` instead of `babel`. Almost the same applies to `typescript` and `babel-ts`. `babel-ts` might support JavaScript features (proposals) not yet supported by TypeScript, but it’s less permissive when it comes to invalid code and less battle-tested than the `typescript` parser.
